{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtMpZASfF7xFw5ugv9Um","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The loops are self-verification cycles: 90% (original) and 99% (E1) of loop cycles contain \"Wait\". Finished answers end the opposite way, e.g. \"Okay. Ready.\", \"I think I've analyzed enough.\", \"I'll write the solution now.\" One finished sample even escaped a short \"Wait, −1/2 = −0.5\" mini-loop and then concluded. So the trap is: finish a check → \"Wait,\" → re-do the same check, copied verbatim and reinforced each cycle. Since removing copy heads doesn't help (copying is redundant), I'll look for components that should counteract repetition. A model trained on natural text normally has copy-suppression heads that see an earlier occurrence and push its logit down. As a first weight-only screen, I'll compute each full-attention head's OV \"copy score\": does attending to token t raise (copying) or lower (suppression) t's own logit? I'll compute it over ~3,000 frequent math-text tokens through the tied embedding. Heads with strongly negative scores are candidate anti-repetition components that could be strengthened.\n\n```python\n# Hypothesis: some FA heads are copy-suppression heads (negative OV self-score); positive-score heads are copiers.\n# token set: frequent tokens in model's own math texts\nfrom collections import Counter\ncnt=Counter()\nfor i in list(TOK.keys())[:150]: cnt.update(TOK[i][:3000])\ntoks=torch.tensor([t for t,_ in cnt.most_common(3000)])\nEt=E[toks]                                  # (T,1024)\ndef ov_copy_score(L, h):\n    ln = 1+load_original(P+f'{L}.input_layernorm.weight')\n    Wv = load_original(P+f'{L}.self_attn.v_proj.weight').view(2,256,1024)[h//4]     # (256,1024)\n    Wo = load_original(P+f'{L}.self_attn.o_proj.weight')[:, h*256:(h+1)*256]       # (1024,256)\n    X = Et*ln; X = X/X.pow(2).mean(-1,keepdim=True).sqrt()\n    out = (X@Wv.T)@Wo.T                       # (T,1024) residual write when attending to token\n    logits = (out*wfin)@Et.T                 # (T,T)\n    z = (logits - logits.mean(1,keepdim=True))/logits.std(1,keepdim=True)\n    diag = z.diag()\n    rank_top = (logits.argmax(1)==torch.arange(len(toks))).float().mean().item()\n    return diag.mean().item(), rank_top\ncs=[]\nfor L in FA:\n    for h in range(8):\n        d,r=ov_copy_score(L,h); cs.append(dict(L=L,h=h,copy_z=d,top1=r))\nCS=pd.DataFrame(cs).set_index(['L','h']).join(S2)\nprint(CS.round(2).to_string())\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3075,"cache_read_input_tokens":109123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3075},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7995bdfb-2bbf-44e3-b05a-b23c0920f67c","uuid":"cf9feecd-0ebb-410a-bdda-ef2f1d1da897","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:13:53.264Z","request_id":"req_011CgtMpYXExxCX78LvcejiD"}
